.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt HALFSVC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halfsvc
.Nd control the HalfBSD Lua userspace service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl socket Ar path
.Ar command
.Op Ar service
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
uses a versioned, bounded Unix-domain JSON protocol.
The default socket is
.Pa /var/run/halfbsd/control.sock .
It prints a JSON response and exits nonzero on a rejected request or timeout.
.Pp
Commands are list, status [service], graph, start service, stop service,
restart service, enable service, disable service, reload and shutdown.
Mutating requests require the manager UID or root, checked with kernel peer
credentials. A service name is validated and is never a shell command.
.Pp
Start/stop/restart requests acknowledge acceptance; use status to observe
asynchronous readiness and termination.
Enable/disable atomically persist preferences across manager restarts and also
start/stop the service. Stop is a current-session activation hold and does not
change persisted enable preferences.
.Pp
Reload preserves the previous registry on validation errors and rejects active
removal/type/dependency changes. Shutdown stops only owned foreground services;
it does not shut down the operating system.
.Pp
Only one request is accepted per connection. Version 1 requests contain version,
command and optional service. Responses contain version, ok and data or error.
No arbitrary expressions, credentials or extra request fields are accepted.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halfinit 8
